        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<figure><img src=\"https://images.theconversation.com/files/748358/original/file-20260716-57-4yz928.jpg?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&amp;rect=0%2C1%2C6452%2C4301&amp;q=45&amp;auto=format&amp;w=1050&amp;h=700&amp;fit=crop\" /><figcaption><span class=\"caption\">Racism was in the news once again at the World Cup. But it comes in many forms.</span> <span class=\"attribution\"><a class=\"source\" href=\"https://www.pexels.com/photo/a-man-sitting-on-a-football-field-5247136/\">Thirdman/Pexels</a></span></figcaption></figure><p>No African teams made it past the quarter-finals of the 2026 menâ€™s football <a href=\"https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/standings\">World Cup</a>, but their strategic and tactical play left a <a href=\"https://novanews.co.za/african-teams-silence-critics-with-strong-world-cup-showing/#google_vignette\">lasting</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/eAF-HVdyWs0\">impression</a>. </p> <p>The success of African teams doesnâ€™t come out of the blue, itâ€™s the result of a long <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/world-cup-history-a-timeline-of-africas-greatest-moments-on-the-field-286908\">process</a>. Itâ€™s therefore surprising that African football remains underrated and downgraded by experts, often in a manner that reveals their ignorance both to African football and history. At times, their comments have a highly problematic racist tone.</p> <p>This was the case with former star player <a href=\"https://www.transfermarkt.co.za/bastian-schweinsteiger/profil/spieler/2514\">Bastian Schweinsteiger</a>, now a longtime commentator for a German TV network. Ahead of a group stage match against CÃ´te dâ€™Ivoire, he was asked what Germanyâ€™s team could expect. He <a hrƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;QXmLEp5bGhGtj9ps-KN4f_GJLcbYdRQ4bfr78X4CTkMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkgcurrentƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///s